the exact L-R identity, re-derived:
   sum_{z in R} d_H(z) = e(L,R) + 2 e(H[R]), and sum_{z in R} d_H(z) = 29|R| - X
   so e(L,R) = 29|R| - X - 2 e(H[R])

their spot check: |R| = 24, blocks (17,12,5), e(H[R]) = 178, row m = 838 so X = 2m - 1624 = 52
   e(L,R) = 29*24 - 52 - 2*178 = 288 (published 288)

composition of the published result:
   903 + 440 = 1343 closed; 8313 - 1343 = 6970 clique-block remaining
   8635 - 1343 = 7292 = 7292 = 6970 + 15 + 307

my ablation of the two halves of inequality 6 (all four runs on the lane own scan):
   both halves off      : 336 closed   (matches their stated baseline)
   w-charge only        : 336 closed   (+0, inert as claimed)
   exact L-side only    : 973 closed   (+637, NOT inert)
   both (as published)  : 1343 closed  (+1007 over the baseline)
   so the w-charge contributes 370 only in combination, and the exact
   L-side is the dominant ingredient on its own.
